514
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:17,453
if you're going to be
part of the family, right?

515
00:33:18,871 --> 00:33:20,122
Part of the family?

516
00:33:21,457 --> 00:33:23,417
I can only hope to be so lucky.

517
00:33:23,834 --> 00:33:27,463
He gets more likable
the more I look at him.

518
00:33:27,546 --> 00:33:30,216
- I know, right?
- Does Yeon-su know

519
00:33:30,966 --> 00:33:32,134
that you're here?

520
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:35,471
I haven't mentioned it to her yet.

521
00:33:36,347 --> 00:33:37,765
Oh, enough with the interrogations.

522
00:33:37,848 --> 00:33:39,892
Let him eat in peace.

523
00:33:40,267 --> 00:33:41,352
- Dig in.
- Right.

524
00:33:41,435 --> 00:33:43,896
Round two is
napa cabbage <i>jeon </i>and <i>makgeolli.</i>

525
00:33:43,979 --> 00:33:45,064
Yes, sir.

526
00:33:46,357 --> 00:33:47,691
He seems clueless, doesn't he?

527
00:33:47,942 --> 00:33:49,985
Have some of the fish too.

528
00:34:01,580 --> 00:34:03,916
- Who is it?
- Delivery.

529
00:34:04,166 --> 00:34:05,209
What?

530
00:34:06,377 --> 00:34:08,379
Si-eun, it's me.

531
00:34:14,301 --> 00:34:15,344
Nam-su?

532
00:34:15,427 --> 00:34:17,596
Why won't you answer my calls
when you were home?

533
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:18,681
You had me worried.

534
00:34:19,848 --> 00:34:23,060
Here, have these. This dumpling place
gets a lot of orders.

535
00:34:23,143 --> 00:34:24,603
I picked some up for you.

536
00:34:25,020 --> 00:34:26,730
Oh, and this.

537
00:34:27,690 --> 00:34:30,109
It's plum extract.
It's supposed to settle your stomach.

538
00:34:35,739 --> 00:34:36,991
What are you

539
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:40,411
- doing right now?
- I'm working a part-time job.

540
00:34:42,705 --> 00:34:44,915
My leg feels better than I expected.

541
00:34:46,208 --> 00:34:47,668
Just eat whatever you crave...

542
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:50,963
until next week.

543
00:34:59,221 --> 00:35:00,306
Si-eun!

544
00:35:01,307 --> 00:35:03,058
Your choice is my choice.

545
00:35:03,726 --> 00:35:06,228
I'll take full responsibility, okay?

546
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:09,356
So don't you worry about a thing.

547
00:35:10,399 --> 00:35:11,400
Okay?

548
00:35:12,735 --> 00:35:14,528
Make sure you heat up
the dumplings before you eat.

549
00:35:15,696 --> 00:35:16,739
All right?

550
00:35:18,949 --> 00:35:19,950
Why...

551
00:35:21,785 --> 00:35:24,246
Why do you always
have to make me the bad one?

552
00:35:53,525 --> 00:35:55,819
Should I have just one glass?

553
00:36:46,203 --> 00:36:47,454
Wait.

554
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:07,766
WHERE DOES YOUR LIFE'S HORIZON LIE?

555
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:16,984
I hit the wrong button.

556
00:37:18,110 --> 00:37:19,486
How do I fix this?

557
00:37:49,308 --> 00:37:50,392
Leave it.

558
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:52,394
It's the lighting setting
I often use.

559
00:37:52,478 --> 00:37:54,646
Oh, the lighting.

560
00:37:54,730 --> 00:37:56,148
Would you like some wine...

561
00:37:57,691 --> 00:37:58,984
I see you already are.

562
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:02,404
I was a bit thirsty.

563
00:38:03,989 --> 00:38:05,699
How about simple pasta for dinner?

564
00:38:06,825 --> 00:38:08,744
Are you a good cook?

565
00:38:09,578 --> 00:38:10,662
Well...

566
00:38:11,663 --> 00:38:12,664
I can manage.

567
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:15,459
So this is

568
00:38:17,085 --> 00:38:19,171
<i>aglio e olio?</i>

569
00:38:19,254 --> 00:38:21,298
Yes, it's <i>aglio e olio.</i>

570
00:38:25,552 --> 00:38:28,722
It should keep the vampires at bay.

571
00:38:30,891 --> 00:38:32,017
Fascinating.

572
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:40,859
Is it that terrible?

573
00:38:44,321 --> 00:38:46,365
You don't cook much, do you?

574
00:38:46,698 --> 00:38:49,952
Truth is, the first thing
I ever cooked after moving here

575
00:38:50,244 --> 00:38:53,372
was the <i>cheonggukjang</i>
your mother gave me.

576
00:38:53,455 --> 00:38:54,456
What?

577
00:38:56,208 --> 00:38:58,669
You actually cooked that?

578
00:38:59,419 --> 00:39:01,255
I normally would've thrown
the ingredient out

579
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:04,216
but for some reason, I really wanted
to try your mother's stew.

580
00:39:05,342 --> 00:39:08,262
Maybe because it was the first time

581
00:39:09,263 --> 00:39:10,347
someone prepared a meal for me.

582
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:15,143
I used to think all that talk

583
00:39:16,144 --> 00:39:18,355
about comfort food and mom's cooking
were nonsense.

584
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:19,690
But I realize now

585
00:39:20,899 --> 00:39:24,528
I just didn't have anyone
to share that connection with.

586
00:39:33,161 --> 00:39:34,371
Can I ask...

587
00:39:36,373 --> 00:39:37,666
why you vanished

588
00:39:38,917 --> 00:39:40,085
that day?

589
00:39:45,048 --> 00:39:46,258
Well...

590
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:52,014
Because you were gone.

591
00:39:57,811 --> 00:39:59,771
It wasn't exactly a surprise, though.

592
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:02,065
We had our fun,
and that's what matters.

593
00:40:06,194 --> 00:40:07,195
We must've missed each other.

594
00:40:08,780 --> 00:40:10,741
I only stepped out
to buy us some breakfast.

595
00:40:15,412 --> 00:40:16,622
It was a first for me.

596
00:40:18,415 --> 00:40:20,334
Wanting to share breakfast

597
00:40:21,501 --> 00:40:23,378
and spend time with someone.

598
00:40:30,218 --> 00:40:31,678
I keep acting out of character...

599
00:40:33,805 --> 00:40:35,432
when I'm around you.

600
00:40:39,019 --> 00:40:41,647
I feel things I never knew existed.

601
00:40:43,357 --> 00:40:45,067
It gives me the courage to do...

602
00:40:53,283 --> 00:40:54,284
I'm sorry.

603
00:40:55,744 --> 00:40:58,330
I'm feeling a bit dizzy.

604
00:40:59,706 --> 00:41:03,335
Give me 30 seconds. No, 1 minute.

605
00:41:23,730 --> 00:41:26,858
Backing down like that
will cost you your territory.

606
00:41:27,693 --> 00:41:29,152
Survival comes first.

607
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:31,279
Sure, you'll survive.

608
00:41:31,613 --> 00:41:32,990
But it takes all the fun out of it.

609
00:41:33,824 --> 00:41:35,701
Are you always this passive
in real life too?

610
00:41:38,954 --> 00:41:40,956
I'm a pacifist by nature, sir.

611
00:41:41,039 --> 00:41:42,958
That's why you let others
take all the credit.

612
00:41:43,041 --> 00:41:47,129
If you back away, your opponent
takes the win. See?

613
00:41:48,005 --> 00:41:49,172
Looks like I lost.

614
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:51,675
Still, I don't regret
the moves I played.

615
00:41:53,176 --> 00:41:54,928
- Come by more often.
- I'm sure

616
00:41:55,012 --> 00:41:57,681
it's much more fun playing
with your friends than with me.

617
00:41:58,306 --> 00:42:01,101
As you saw,
my play style is pretty boring.

618
00:42:01,184 --> 00:42:02,185
True.

619
00:42:03,061 --> 00:42:04,229
But they're

620
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:06,148
all gone now.

621
00:42:07,190 --> 00:42:08,400
Gone where?

622
00:42:17,868 --> 00:42:19,369
- Another game?
- Sure.

623
00:42:49,107 --> 00:42:50,692
Get some shut-eye.

624
00:42:51,151 --> 00:42:52,402
I'll wake you up in an hour.

625
00:42:55,363 --> 00:42:57,199
So are we

626
00:42:58,075 --> 00:43:00,619
doing it now?

627
00:43:06,792 --> 00:43:10,253
I can't. I'm wearing
mismatched underwear today.

628
00:43:15,050 --> 00:43:16,051
Die.

629
00:43:17,260 --> 00:43:19,262
Just die.

630
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:21,932
Where's my phone?

631
00:43:25,018 --> 00:43:26,228
What time is it?

632
00:43:29,439 --> 00:43:30,774
I'm dead for real.

633
00:43:50,252 --> 00:43:51,753
I'm sorry.

634
00:43:51,837 --> 00:43:53,964
I meant to wake you, but I dozed off.

635
00:43:54,047 --> 00:43:55,757
It's fine. Go on upstairs and sleep.

636
00:43:55,841 --> 00:43:57,217
I need to hurry out.

637
00:43:57,759 --> 00:43:59,886
Let me drive you home.

638
00:44:08,061 --> 00:44:09,104
What time is it?

639
00:44:14,442 --> 00:44:16,528
Oh, my arm.

640
00:44:17,863 --> 00:44:19,781
My body is aching all over.

641
00:44:27,414 --> 00:44:28,415
Goodness.

642
00:44:30,750 --> 00:44:32,669
Baek-hee... Gosh, you scared me.

643
00:44:33,336 --> 00:44:36,423
Wait. Have you been here
this whole time?

644
00:44:37,090 --> 00:44:39,593
Yeon-su... Has Yeon-su come back?

645
00:44:40,677 --> 00:44:42,721
Jeez.

646
00:44:43,638 --> 00:44:46,349
Why is she
working overtime this late?

647
00:44:47,726 --> 00:44:50,604
Baek-hee, go inside
and get some sleep.

648
00:44:50,687 --> 00:44:52,439
I'll wake you up when she gets back.

649
00:44:54,524 --> 00:44:58,236
I know kids follow
their own destinies

650
00:44:59,487 --> 00:45:02,532
but I never expected her
to cross the line this quietly.

651
00:45:05,827 --> 00:45:09,831
It makes me wonder
if I was too strict with her.

652
00:45:09,915 --> 00:45:11,917
Why would that be your fault?

653
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:14,211
You know how the Gongs are.

654
00:45:14,294 --> 00:45:17,005
They go all the way once they set
their minds on something.

655
00:45:17,088 --> 00:45:18,506
It's in the genes.

656
00:45:19,299 --> 00:45:23,970
She's just carrying
on the family tradition faithfully.

657
00:45:29,643 --> 00:45:31,728
Anyway, isn't the floor
uncomfortable for him?

658
00:45:32,854 --> 00:45:34,898
Why is he sleeping there
instead of going home?

659
00:45:39,277 --> 00:45:40,987
How many bottles of <i>makgeolli</i>
did they drink?

660
00:45:41,404 --> 00:45:43,990
Seriously, Father is unbelievable.

661
00:45:50,789 --> 00:45:52,499
Hey, Nam-su.

662
00:45:52,832 --> 00:45:54,751
Yeon-su? Dal?

663
00:45:56,544 --> 00:45:58,421
Are you just getting home now?

664
00:45:58,588 --> 00:46:00,048
What's going on?
Did you guys sleep out?

665
00:46:00,131 --> 00:46:01,216
- I worked...
- She fell asleep.

666
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:05,220
That was horrible timing.

667
00:46:06,388 --> 00:46:08,431
She fell asleep while working late.

668
00:46:08,515 --> 00:46:10,267
I see you still can't get
your stories straight.

669
00:46:10,350 --> 00:46:12,727
- Whatever. Just get over the wall.
- Me?

670
00:46:13,561 --> 00:46:14,646
Wait, me?

671
00:46:17,649 --> 00:46:19,526
I'm still feeling a bit sore too.

672
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:25,407
- Dal.
- What?

673
00:46:25,490 --> 00:46:26,992
Hey, no way.

674
00:46:27,075 --> 00:46:29,411
Hop over quickly
and open the gate for us.

675
00:46:30,120 --> 00:46:31,830
No, you can go home. We'll manage.

676
00:46:31,913 --> 00:46:33,873
Look at us.
How are we going to manage?

677
00:46:33,957 --> 00:46:36,001
Dal, you're tall.

678
00:46:36,084 --> 00:46:38,003
You've got the legs
to swing right over.

679
00:46:38,086 --> 00:46:41,673
We can't possibly ask my boss
to hop a wall.

680
00:46:56,855 --> 00:46:57,856
Oh, wow.

681
00:47:03,778 --> 00:47:05,071
Dal.

682
00:47:05,613 --> 00:47:08,283
You just need to push
that wooden latch to the side.

683
00:47:09,242 --> 00:47:12,912
Why on earth are you hopping our wall

684
00:47:13,788 --> 00:47:15,290
at this time of night?

685
00:47:16,166 --> 00:47:17,167
Ma'am.

686
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:21,838
Gosh, I'm tired.

687
00:47:25,884 --> 00:47:27,927
- Dal?
- Ji-o?

688
00:47:28,511 --> 00:47:29,721
What are you doing here?

689
00:47:31,598 --> 00:47:33,391
And what are you doing there?

690
00:47:33,475 --> 00:47:34,601
This won't do.

691
00:47:34,684 --> 00:47:36,436
- Give me your back.
- My back?

692
00:47:58,500 --> 00:48:01,252
Mom...

693
00:48:01,336 --> 00:48:02,545
Ms. Gong.

694
00:48:03,797 --> 00:48:04,798
Mr. Yun?

695
00:48:06,466 --> 00:48:07,509
Nam-su.

696
00:48:09,010 --> 00:48:10,762
Yeon-su, we need to talk.

697
00:48:18,645 --> 00:48:19,771
What do we do?

698
00:48:24,901 --> 00:48:26,986
All of you, please follow me.

699
00:48:29,155 --> 00:48:31,074
This is not good at all.

700
00:48:41,209 --> 00:48:42,335
Explain yourself.

701
00:48:43,670 --> 00:48:49,426
Work ended late tonight,
so Mr. Dokgo drove me home.

702
00:48:49,509 --> 00:48:50,760
I won't ask twice.

703
00:48:51,469 --> 00:48:52,470
Which one is it?

704
00:48:53,138 --> 00:48:54,139
What?

705
00:48:56,391 --> 00:48:58,017
What do you mean, which one?

706
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:03,064
- Which of the two is it?
- Who are you talking about?

707
00:49:03,148 --> 00:49:05,400
Anyway, why were you sleeping here?

708
00:49:05,483 --> 00:49:07,819
I had <i>makgeolli </i>with Mr. Gong
and passed out.

709
00:49:07,902 --> 00:49:10,155
Why were you hopping the wall?

710
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:13,700
- The gate was locked, so I did.
- Shush, I can't hear them.

711
00:49:13,783 --> 00:49:14,826
Keep it down, will you?

712
00:49:21,416 --> 00:49:22,834
What is this?

713
00:49:22,917 --> 00:49:24,669
You tell me.

714
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:27,422
There must be a reason
you're reading this book.

715
00:49:33,845 --> 00:49:35,138
You're pregnant!

716
00:49:36,681 --> 00:49:40,268
What? I'm what?

717
00:49:40,351 --> 00:49:42,687
You little punk,
when the heck did you...

718
00:49:46,566 --> 00:49:49,694
Mom, don't tell me
you seriously think this is mine...

719
00:49:49,777 --> 00:49:51,571
Tell me the truth. Who is the father?

720
00:49:53,615 --> 00:49:55,408
Yeon-su, just spit it out.

721
00:49:55,492 --> 00:49:57,160
Is it number 1 or 2?
It's number 2, right?

722
00:49:57,243 --> 00:49:59,829
- No, never.
- Which number am I?

723
00:49:59,913 --> 00:50:02,040
Absolutely not. I swear, Mom.

724
00:50:02,123 --> 00:50:04,751
Then, why did I find this book
under your bed?

725
00:50:04,834 --> 00:50:06,586
What? You found this

726
00:50:07,629 --> 00:50:10,048
under my bed?

727
00:50:14,719 --> 00:50:16,513
That little brat...

728
00:50:25,897 --> 00:50:28,525
Mom, listen to me for a second.

729
00:50:28,608 --> 00:50:30,443
- Gong Yeon-su!
- It's Gong Nam-su!

730
00:50:30,527 --> 00:50:32,654
It's not me.
Nam-su's girlfriend is pregnant.

731
00:50:32,737 --> 00:50:33,780
You traitor!

732
00:50:34,739 --> 00:50:36,783
You've brought shame
upon our ancestors!

733
00:50:36,866 --> 00:50:39,911
No, you've brought shame upon me.

734
00:50:39,994 --> 00:50:42,413
- How dare you hide it under my bed?
- Ms. Gong.

735
00:50:43,331 --> 00:50:44,624
Jeez.

736
00:50:47,126 --> 00:50:48,878
This truth battle is crazy.

737
00:50:52,882 --> 00:50:55,635
- Nam-su, you...
- I'm sorry, Mother.

738
00:50:55,718 --> 00:50:57,011
It just happened.

739
00:51:00,974 --> 00:51:02,100
What the...

740
00:51:05,270 --> 00:51:07,647
Mom! Yeon-su works
at a sex toy company.

741
00:51:08,064 --> 00:51:10,608
And the two of them
spent the night together!

742
00:51:11,234 --> 00:51:12,735
- Hey, you...
- Is that true?

743
00:51:18,616 --> 00:51:19,909
Yeon-su, answer me!

744
00:51:28,793 --> 00:51:29,919
I like her.

745
00:51:40,722 --> 00:51:41,848
I have

746
00:51:42,765 --> 00:51:44,225
feelings for Ms. Gong.

747
00:52:01,784 --> 00:52:05,830
MAKE ME TINGLE
